      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T20:01:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not a new issue, but tsh-\u003ehdr_size and tsh-\u003epercpu_data_size is in a memory region writable by another OS. It should not be trusted here.",
      "revId": "b4350f67cea8b6f4f8ad4cc9e4b0a46823abd095",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34acdb61_57a101ac",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-sched-share.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T20:01:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This might work right now, but the ff-a spec defines 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF as an invalid id, not 0. Although it does also require passing 0 as the id in APIs where it has not yet been allocated, I do not see any requirement that the SPM does not use 0 also as a valid handle.",
      "revId": "b4350f67cea8b6f4f8ad4cc9e4b0a46823abd095",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c910cf68_132190e8",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-sched-share.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 226,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T20:01:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should probably also call this if you don\u0027t have a valid sched_shared_mem_id. I don\u0027t like your current init flow though. trusty_register_sched_share allocates resources that you don\u0027t free if SMC_SC_SCHED_SHARE_REGISTER fails. I think trusty_unregister_sched_share should undo everything trusty_register_sched_share did and if trusty_register_sched_share fails, it should go back to the state it was in before. If you are leaving the extra buffers allocated anyway, why defer the allocation at all.",
      "revId": "b4350f67cea8b6f4f8ad4cc9e4b0a46823abd095",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aedb4d6a_4198af4e",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-sched-share.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 226,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T20:05:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that if trusty_register_sched_share but also fail to reclaim the memory, you will need remember that, and don\u0027t call vfree in trusty_free_sched_share.",
